WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.450
Yesterday, one of you asked

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.970
me a big question.

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.940
“Will AI take my mum’s job?”

4
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:08.690
She’s a nurse.

5
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.410
Let’s find an honest answer:

6
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.650
no hype, and no fear.

7
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.660
Today: how AI changes work, the new work

8
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.280
it creates, and skills worth building.

9
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.060
A job is a bundle of tasks.

10
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.840
A nurse checks patients, writes

11
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.620
notes and talks with families.

12
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.400
AI can help with some: turning speech into

13
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.720
notes, or flagging a worrying reading.

14
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.330
It can’t calm a frightened child.

15
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.130
So AI usually changes

16
00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.510
tasks, not whole jobs.

17
00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.910
Honestly, some jobs will shrink, and

18
00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.230
people will need new skills.

19
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.320
But AI also creates work.

20
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.580
Someone has to label data, like photos of

21
00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.700
sick crops or Hausa voice recordings:

22
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.540
real work that deserves fair pay.

23
00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:05.260
Others build models, test

24
00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.540
them and fix them.

25
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:08.720
Two words help here.

26
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.220
Automation: AI does a task instead of

27
00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.160
a person, like sorting spam.

28
00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.060
Augmentation: AI helps a person do it

29
00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.940
better, like an alert for a nurse.

30
00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.230
Most changes mix the two.

31
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.630
Think of mobile money.

32
00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.600
Market traders didn’t

33
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.980
disappear when it arrived.

34
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.180
Counting cash took less time, and a

35
00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.400
new job appeared on every corner:

36
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.240
the mobile money agent.

37
00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.610
AI is a bigger change, but

38
00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.150
often works the same way.

39
00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:41.730
Quick check!

40
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.950
A hospital starts using AI to turn

41
00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.970
doctors’ spoken notes into text.

42
00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.380
What’s most likely to happen?

43
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.260
Some of their tasks change.

44
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.080
Doctors type less and spend

45
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.440
more time with patients.

46
00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:59.530
But someone still checks the notes,

47
00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:03.370
because AI can mishear a name or a dose.

48
00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.930
AI work is already near you.

49
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.900
On farms, apps spot crop

50
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.360
disease from leaf photos.

51
00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.900
In clinics, AI helps read X-rays.

52
00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.640
Planners use it to set bus routes.

53
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.640
And people train voice typing for

54
00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.480
Yoruba, Swahili and Bangla.

55
00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.710
So which skills should you build?

56
00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.970
Maths and data, to

57
00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.550
understand what AI does.

58
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.120
Judging information, to

59
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.000
check what it says.

60
00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.250
Ethics, to ask whether it should.

61
00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.840
And working with people, which

62
00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.380
no AI can do for you.

63
00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.290
In the app, you’re the planner:

64
00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.330
place your school’s bus stops.

65
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.250
Every house joins its nearest stop, every

66
00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.170
stop moves to the middle of its houses,

67
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.870
and neighbourhoods appear by themselves.

68
00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.070
But you choose how many

69
00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.150
stops: a human decision.

70
00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:00.990
Your turn.

71
00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.840
As AI spreads, which skill becomes more

72
00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.340
valuable: memorising facts, or judging

73
00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.120
whether information is true?

74
00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:14.960
Judging information: AI produces facts in

75
00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.700
seconds, but someone must check them.

76
00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.530
Remember: AI mostly changes

77
00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.550
tasks, not whole jobs.

78
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.660
It creates new work too, from

79
00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.400
labelling data to testing.

80
00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.550
And build data skills,

81
00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.070
judgement, ethics and teamwork.

82
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.380
Try it yourself: interview an

83
00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.540
adult about their work.

84
00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.720
Ask for one task AI could help

85
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.220
with, and one it never should.

86
00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:45.070
Then ask them why, and write

87
00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:45.870
down what they say.
